  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits a strong upward drift bias when recent history shows volatility or prior spikes; true outcomes frequently reverse direction within the first 3-5 days of the forecast horizon.",
    "When sentiment is near zero (0.00) but price history contains a spike, the model fails to account for mean reversion risk and overestimates the next period's level.",
    "The model systematically ignores short-term volatility clustering; true outcomes often show high variance (spikes followed by drops) while forecasts produce smooth, linearly increasing paths.",
    "Forecasts are overly sensitive to the most recent price point but ignore the momentum reversal signal present in the preceding 5-7 days of history.",
    "In low-sentiment environments, the model fails to capture sudden mean-reversion events that occur after a short-term peak, resulting in significant overvaluation by day 10-20."
  ]
}
